# Brand assets are binary: never diffed, never line-ending-converted (docs/assets/README.md).
*.gif  binary
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary

# Agent-facing, and only that: in the repository, never in an archive. `git archive` honours this,
# and both the artifact packager (eval/artifact/make_artifact.sh) and GitHub's zip download use it.
#
# `.github/` deliberately STAYS in the archive: `ci.yml` is the only place that documents building
# the engine with no GPU and no CUDA toolkit (the libcuda stub, the AOT compile for one arch), and
# that is evidence an artifact evaluator wants rather than clutter.
#
# Adding a line here is also a promise to reword whatever names the file: it vanishes from every
# tarball while staying in the checkout, so a reference to it dangles for everyone who unpacks one
# and looks fine here. tests/repo/test_docs_hygiene.py enforces that.
CLAUDE.md export-ignore
